  "query_preview": "the Extreme Heat Warning for these areas through Tuesday.\nVery warm overnight lows and high temps into the 100-105 range \ncontinue in far eastern Montana and Sheridan County Wy into\nWednesday...and for these areas we have extended the Extreme Heat\nWarning through Wednesday. \n\nOtherwise, highs in the lower to mid 90s will be common through \nthe remainder of the week. Models indicate monsoonal moisture will\nslide into our region from the southwest with hints of occasional\nweak impulses in the mean flow. At a minimum, this looks to bring\nan increase in relative humidity, with a moderate chance of daily\nshowers/thunderstorms for the area. Ensembles have stubbornly\nstuck to their remarkable PWAT progs, reaching up to 1.50 inches \nin the area from Tuesday onward. So any decent impulse in the \nmonsoonal flow may result in storms with locally heavy rainfall. \n\nFire weather...Elevated to critical fire weather conditions are \nexpected for most locations today due to the combination of hot \ntemperatures, very dry conditions (afternoon humidity down into \nthe single digits and teens) and breezy winds. Expect breezy south\nto southwest winds to develop over the area (gusts 20s to 30s \nmph) this afternoon, ahead of the aforementioned cold front this \nevening/night. There is a small chance (10% or less) of a few \nhigh-based showers/virga developing over our western areas by \nlate afternoon and evening. A Red Flag Warning is in effect \nthrough 9 pm this evening for most areas. Elevated conditions may \nlinger in our east overnight (especially along ridges) due to a \nlow level jet and slow RH recovery as the weak front slides over \nthe area. Please take care not to cause a spark or do any burning.\nBT",
